-- title:
--   Mod-varpi local rings of the j-finite chart are DVRs
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime and $M$ a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$. Let $L$ be a field of characteristic zero that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ of order $p$, and let $\zeta \in L$ be a primitive $p$-th root of unity. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with an $L$-algebra structure for which $L$ is the fraction field of $A$, such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A \to L$, and let $\varpi \in A$ generate the maximal ideal. Let $K_M$ be an intermediate field of $L((q))/L$, equipped with a compatible $A$-algebra structure over $L$, equal to the $L$-subfield of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ L$ generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field $\mathtt{x1FunctionFieldC}\ \mathbb{Q}\ (\Gamma_1(M)) \subseteq \mathbb{Q}((q))$, and let $j_M \in K_M$ be an element, assumed nonzero, whose underlying Laurent series is the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion $\mathtt{jq}$ of the modular invariant $j$. Write $B = \mathtt{chartAlgFin}\ A\ K_M\ j_M$ for the subalgebra of $K_M$ consisting of the elements integral over $A[j_M] = \mathrm{Algebra.adjoin}\ A\ \{j_M\}$. Then for every maximal ideal $\mathfrak{m}$ of $B$ containing the image of $\varpi$, the quotient of the localisation $B_{\mathfrak{m}}$ by the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi$ is a domain and a discrete valuation ring; the conclusion is packaged as the existence of the domain instance together with the discrete valuation ring statement for that quotient.
--
--   This is the assertion that the special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(M)$ over $A$ is a smooth curve, read at a closed point of its $j$-finite chart: the local ring of the fibre is a one-dimensional regular local ring. It supplies the domain and discrete-valuation-ring instances for $B_{\mathfrak m}/(\varpi)$ used by [`ModularCurve.XOne.finite_and_flat_chartAlgFin_levelRaise_x1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOne.finite_and_flat_chartAlgFin_levelRaise_x1) and by [`ModularCurve.XOne.isDiscreteValuationRing_and_isFractionRing_of_mem_iff_exists_mul_residue_eq_x1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XOne.isDiscreteValuationRing_and_isFractionRing_of_mem_iff_exists_mul_residue_eq_x1).
